  "_puffery_alternatives_note": "NB502: the plain word the buzzword is standing in for. A closed set — every key is a term already on the 'puffery' list, so this adds suggestions without widening what gets flagged. Deliberately NOT a general thesaurus: a broad synonym source returns the wrong sense and the wrong register, and one bad suggestion costs more trust than a missing one buys. Matching is by lemma, so the rule only offers these as a drop-in substitution when the writer used the base form verbatim ('delve' → 'examine'); an inflected hit ('delved') becomes a rewrite, because the alternatives are listed uninflected.",
